#edb/ref 1083 #uuid "929258e4-1ed5-5b7d-8880-aba10bed2194" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276852 #edb/ref 1080 "12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276852 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276852 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "992c7b81-3eb7-55dc-bc8c-3bd914085869" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276920 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276920 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276920 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a0222e17-38e9-574c-9fce-ece43f8640e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277436 #edb/ref 1080 "3{e}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277436 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277436 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e0656531-5f92-50c3-8174-7a4c5b980686" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277458 #edb/ref 1080 "3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277458 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277458 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e255bf4d-f521-5b32-8e26-405c65c4a7ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277593 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{e}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277593 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277593 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f106b996-8990-5fef-94a8-8ae99ae28da6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276920 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277997 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277997 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277997 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186276920 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277997 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9950b528-93fa-5fe7-a6ea-a3f27b30d432" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278031 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278031 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278031 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186276804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278031 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "afb72719-6e3d-599c-8a5a-a7d44b4323e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278307 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278307 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160463" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278307 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278307 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}},\\, & x\\ge -2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278307 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4ee7fd8-9373-59cf-bc78-d62531a54190" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278307 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}}$ on the interval $x\\ge -2,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{k}{6(x+3)^{6}}\\,{|}_{-2}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{6}=1\\,⟹\\,k=6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278310 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278310 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160467" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278310 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278310 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{3x+2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278310 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "008eb439-04f8-52ac-8507-0ab3780bebdf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278310 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{3x+2}$ on the interval $x\\le 0,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}k{e}^{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}k{e}^{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{k}{3}{e}^{3x+2}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0}=\\frac{k{e}^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k{e}^{2}}{3}=1\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{3}{{e}^{2}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186421867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186421868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186421869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421852 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421852 #edb/ref 1045 "Continuous Random Variables Over Infinite Domains" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421852 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186421869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421852 #edb/ref 